Lemma 26: f(f(X, f(f(f(Y, Z), X), Y)), f(f(f(Y, X), X), f(f(f(Y, Z), X), Y))) = Y.
Proof:
  f(f(X, f(f(f(Y, Z), X), Y)), f(f(f(Y, X), X), f(f(f(Y, Z), X), Y)))
