Lemma 29: f(f(f(X, Y), f(Y, Y)), X) = f(f(X, Y), f(f(Y, X), Y)).
Proof:
  f(f(f(X, Y), f(Y, Y)), X)
= { by axiom 1 (hyp) }
  f(f(f(X, Y), f(Y, Y)), f(f(f(Y, f(X, Y)), f(f(X, Y), f(X, Y))), Y))
= { by lemma 25 }
  f(f(X, Y), f(f(Y, f(f(f(Y, f(X, Y)), f(f(X, Y), f(X, Y))), Y)), Y))
= { by axiom 1 (hyp) R->L }
  f(f(X, Y), f(f(Y, X), Y))

Lemma 30: f(f(f(X, f(X, f(X, X))), f(X, f(X, f(X, X)))), X) = f(f(f(X, X), f(X, X)), X).
Proof:
