Lemma 31: f(f(X, f(Y, X)), f(f(f(Y, X), X), f(Y, X))) = f(f(f(X, Y), f(f(Y, X), Y)), X).
Proof:
  f(f(X, f(Y, X)), f(f(f(Y, X), X), f(Y, X)))
